Third-party data

worldgen/data/giant_optics.npz
  Methane absorption cross sections derived from the table of Karkoschka, E.
  1994, Icarus 111, 174 (doi:10.1006/icar.1994.1139), with scattering
  properties of cloud and haze particles computed by Mie theory. The file is
  built by scripts/build_giant_optics.py. The table is also distributed by the
  MPI-Mainz UV/VIS Spectral Atlas (Keller-Rudek, H. et al. 2013, Earth Syst.
  Sci. Data 5, 365, doi:10.5194/essd-5-365-2013); the atlas page for it gives
  no licence.

Statistics and values from published work

The package includes no other third-party data files. Numerical values taken
from published work are written in worldgen/heuristics.py and the validation
scripts with their sources, which are listed in docs/references.md. Two
sources provide values computed from published data sets:

  PHOIBLE 2.0 (Moran, S., McCloy, D. & Forkel, R. 2019, doi:10.5281/zenodo.2626687).
  The share of the 3020 inventories that contain each consonant, and the
  share with a long vowel, set the weights used to draw sound inventories for
  invented languages. The PHOIBLE web site gives the licence as CC BY-SA 3.0
  and the Zenodo record as CC BY 3.0. The package contains these aggregate
  shares and none of the PHOIBLE tables.

  HYDE 3.2 (Klein Goldewijk, K. et al. 2017, doi:10.5194/essd-9-927-2017).
  Global population totals at selected dates serve as targets for the
  simulated history. The package contains these totals and none of the HYDE
  grids.

Dependencies

The dependencies listed in pyproject.toml are installed separately and keep
their own licences (BSD, MIT, Apache-2.0 and the matplotlib licence).
